From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:05:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 089/342] meson_hdmi: DPMS, and 720p50, 1080p24, 1080p25 and
 1080p50

DPMS: anything but on stops the encoder and switches the PHY's TMDS
output off, as Linux's meson_dw_hdmi does, so the display sees no signal
and can sleep; on gives the PHY its setting back and programs the mode
again, as a mode switch does. The accelerant reports standby, suspend
and off, so the screen saver's "Turn off screen" now works.

Modes: the ones U-Boot's two pixel clocks (74.25 and 148.5 MHz) give
with longer lines: 720p50, 1080p24, 1080p25 and 1080p50. As before, a
mode is offered when the display's EDID lists it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
